Source: aurora-firmware
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Aurora Silicon <noreply@aurorasilicon.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/debian-aurora
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: aurora-firmware
Architecture: all
Depends: asahi-scripts, dracut, kmod, wireless-regdb, cpio, util-linux, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Admit Apple Silicon peripherals after their firmware is extracted
 Peripherals that need the Mac's own firmware (the always-on processor, the
 MT7932 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, DockChannel keyboards) are kept from loading
 until the initrd has extracted that firmware from the EFI system partition;
 a dracut module and a boot service then load them explicitly.
